1
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Valhalla Rising is a adventure, drama, action film
directed by Nicolas Winding Refn.

2
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Scandinavia, 1,000 AD.

3
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:03,000
For years, One Eye, a mute warrior of supernatural strength, has
been held prisoner by the Norse chieftain Barde.

4
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Aided by Are, a boy slave, One Eye slays his captor and together he and
Are escape, beginning a journey into the heart of darkness.

5
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
On their flight, One Eye and Are board a Viking vessel, but the ship is soon engulfed
by an endless fog that clears only as the crew sights an unknown land.

6
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:00,000
As the new world reveals its secrets and the Vikings confront their
terrible and bloody fate, One Eye discovers his true self.

7
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:39,000
One-Eye, played by Mads Mikkelsen.

8
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Kare, played by Gary Lewis.

9
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:57,000
Gorm, played by Jamie Sives.

10
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Eirik, played by Ewan Stewart.

11
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:15,000
Barde, played by Alexander Morton.

12
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
Pagan Viking Guard, played by Callum Mitchell.

13
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:33,000
Valhalla Rising is a 2009 English-language Danish period adventure film directed by Nicolas
Winding Refn, co-written by Refn and Roy Jacobsen, and starring Mads Mikkelsen.

14
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:12,000
The film takes place "most certainly during the twelfth century of our era", and follows a Norse warrior named One-Eye
and a boy as they travel with a band of Christian Crusaders by ship in the hopes of finding the Holy Land.

15
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
Instead, they find themselves in North America where they
are assailed by Natives and dark visions.

16
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
Shot entirely in Scotland, the title is derived from the combination of Kenneth
Anger's films Scorpio Rising and Lucifer Rising with a Viking theme.

17
01:19:03,000 --> 01:19:09,000
While the film garnered generally positive reviews, it only made back
about $731,613 of its $5.7 million production cost.

18
01:23:42,000 --> 01:23:48,000
The film explores themes of escape, hell, mythology, surreal, gore.

19
01:28:21,000 --> 01:28:27,000
The tone is dark and emotional and mind_bending.
